    bw3   cell 0    0.000  ->  cell 2   -0.018   delta   -0.018 +-  0.011  flat (not required of a bandwidth)

  CLAUSE 2 -- THE POSITIVE CONTROL: the ear demonstrably resolves f1 and
  f2, so both must clear the 2AFC bar in ALL FOUR CELLS or the ruler is
  wrong. (§41's extra demand that they not MOVE with the gain is withdrawn:
  bw1 and bw2 ARE the f1/f2 resonators' bandwidths, so render_bw_gain moves
  them by design. The first build voided here and was right to.)
    f3=0 bw=0   f1 d'  6.881   f2 d'  9.469   -> ok
    f3=1 bw=0   f1 d'  6.101   f2 d'  8.982   -> ok
    f3=0 bw=1   f1 d'  6.643   f2 d' 10.182   -> ok
    f3=1 bw=1   f1 d'  6.186   f2 d'  9.536   -> ok

  CLAUSE 3 -- THE TEST: each axis in ITS OWN cell, as a fraction of F1's
  d' there. Bar: d' >= 1.0 (~76% in a 2AFC) AND significantly above zero at
  2.447 x the paired SE, because a 2AFC bar inside the estimator's own noise
  is not a bar. Ratios are taken in d', NOT d'^2 -- run 1's were squares.
    f1   f3=0 bw=0  d'^2   47.345 +-  0.932   d'  6.881   1.000 x F1   50.8 sd   -> AUDIBLE
    f2   f3=0 bw=0  d'^2   89.670 +-  1.774   d'  9.469   1.376 x F1   50.6 sd   -> AUDIBLE
    f3   f3=1 bw=0  d'^2   23.539 +-  0.328   d'  4.852   0.795 x F1   71.8 sd   -> AUDIBLE
    bw1  f3=0 bw=1  d'^2    0.610 +-  0.042   d'  0.781   0.118 x F1   14.4 sd   -> REAL BUT SUB-BAR
    bw2  f3=0 bw=1  d'^2    0.766 +-  0.068   d'  0.875   0.132 x F1   11.2 sd   -> REAL BUT SUB-BAR
    bw3  f3=1 bw=1  d'^2    0.345 +-  0.021   d'  0.588   0.095 x F1   16.3 sd   -> REAL BUT SUB-BAR

  CLAUSE 4 -- THE ATTRIBUTION of F1's cost, paired over 12 reps, t = 2.447.
  Run 1 moved both gains at once and so could not say which one paid.
    f3 alone      dd'^2  -10.127 +-  0.324   -> COSTS F1
    bw alone      dd'^2   -3.211 +-  0.245   -> COSTS F1
    both (corner) dd'^2   -9.083 +-  0.284   -> real
    interaction   dd'^2    4.255 +-  0.204   -> present

  1 OF THE FOUR NEW AXES ARE AUDIBLE at their own reach, so the air
  carries them and stage 2b -- whether the auditory MODULE represents
  them -- is worth building. STILL NOT A WORD COUNT: this says the
  distinction survives the cochlea, not that the creature uses it, and
  kVLScoreFormant still scores only F1/F2.

  AND 3 AXES ARE REAL BUT SUB-BAR, which run 1 got wrong in BOTH
  directions at once. Its over-strict floor hid that they are resolvably
  non-zero, and its squared ratio made them look ~10x weaker than they
  are. They are not inaudible; they are WEAK -- roughly a tenth of F1 in
  d', about 67% in a 2AFC against 50% chance. That is below the bar for a
  teachable level and well above nothing, so they stay OFF and stay OPEN:
  an axis at a tenth of F1 could clear the bar at a larger reach, and the
  reach here is the one §41 run 1 measured, not a limit of the body.

  THE SHIP DECISION, ON THE ATTRIBUTION RATHER THAN THE CORNER:
  BOTH GAINS COST F1, so there is no free pick: the third formant is a
  trade against the first and the prize arithmetic must price it.
WALL 24.86 s
